; Neonmancer push motifs: small original patterns that only work under the
; game's rules (he climbs crates and 1-high blocks, jumps 1-tile holes,
; crates plug holes, fall off ledges and stack). Each is solved with
; scripts/solve.mjs; the numbers are its output. Characters: see xsb.mjs.
; Copy the idea, not the cells: a room sets it in its own shape.

; Bridge and weight: the plate lies past a row of holes he can jump but a
; crate can't cross. The trick: plug the hole in the plate's own column,
; then the second crate rolls over the first. Plugging any other column
; spends a crate for nothing. 8 pushes, 2 sharp steps, 86% traps (solve.mjs).
#########
#33.3333#
#^^^^^^^#
#       #
# $  $  #
#   @   #
#########

; Stack stairs: the way out is on a 3-high wall, two blocks above any
; step he has. The trick: push the floor crate under the ledge's edge
; first, then push the ledge crate off onto it: a 2-high stack beside the
; wall. Dropping the ledge crate first (the obvious push) is the trap.
; 7 pushes, 1 sharp step (the first), 69% traps (solve.mjs).
; exit: +x:0:3
#########
#111& 33#
#1111 33#
#       #
# $     #
#  @    #
#########
